---
description: Do not auto-commit when solving issues or tickets
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Auto-Commit on Issues/Tickets

When solving an issue or a Linear ticket, **do not** create a git commit automatically.
Let the user review the changes first and only commit when explicitly asked.

# No Amend-and-Push Unless Instructed

**Never** amend a commit and force-push unless the user explicitly asks you to amend.
Always create a new commit instead. Only amend when the user says "amend".

# No Ticket IDs in Commits or PR Titles

**Do not** append Linear ticket numbers (e.g. `[PINT-123]`) to commit messages or PR titles.
Reference tickets only in the PR description body.
